        <h1 class="post-detail__title">Youth Philanthropy in Action</h1>

        <div class="post-detail__featured-image">
          <img src="/assets/images/news/49895.png" alt="Youth Philanthropy in Action" loading="lazy">
        </div>

        <div class="post-detail__content">
          <p>Part of the <strong>Tin Cup Challenger Fund</strong> goes directly to support the Youth Philanthropy Program at Teton High School. Now in its <strong>10th year</strong>, this fall&#8217;s participating seniors have <strong>16 grant applications</strong> to weigh over the course of two class periods, with a total ask of nearly <strong>$14,000</strong>. With the additional generosity of Challenger Richard Grundler, this year students have a total of <strong>$7,000 to award</strong>.</p>

<p>This program illustrates real-world philanthropy on a local level while shedding light on Teton Valley&#8217;s nonprofit landscape and current community needs. &nbsp;<strong>Your support&nbsp;</strong>provides graduating seniors with&nbsp;insight into the many benefits philanthropy has to offer as they become&nbsp;emerging community leaders themselves.</p>

<p>Students are currently discussing grant applications and looking forward to an&nbsp;<strong>Awards Ceremony</strong>&nbsp;scheduled for the end of the month at Teton High School. Thank you for supporting this program!</p>

<p>Youth Philanthropy Program explained in 3 minutes!</p>
